<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>XSS Lab - HTML Context Reflection</title>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>XSS Lab: Identify & Break HTML Context</h1>

  <p>
    In this lab, whatever you type will be reflected back into the page.  
    Try to figure out **what context your input is reflected in** and then  
    **break the context properly** to execute your XSS payload.
  </p>

  <form method="GET">
    <input type="text" name="q" placeholder="Enter something...">
    <button type="submit">Submit</button>
  </form>

  <h2>Output:</h2>
  <p>
    You searched for: 
    <span id="output"></span>
  </p>

  <script>
    // get query param "q"
    const params = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search);
    const q = params.get("q");

    // directly reflect user input without sanitization (intentionally vulnerable)
    if (q) {
      document.getElementById("output").innerHTML = q;
    }
  </script>
</body>
</html>
